  "lights": {
    "default": false,
    "unverified": true,
    "note": "Set LED mode to External in Korg's editor first (KORG KONTROL Editor: Common, LED Mode, External, then write the scene to the controller); until then the lights follow the buttons and ignore the box. Lit: there is something here; slowly pulsing: it is the one on now. Unverified: Korg's guide names the mode, not the messages, and which buttons have a light (S, M, R, Cycle and the five transport buttons here) is from descriptions, not from a real unit.",
    "sources": ["Korg nanoKONTROL2 Parameter Guide (E1), 'LED Mode [Internal, External]', p. 9: in External mode a button's LED follows a message from the computer with the control change number assigned to that button", "Secondary: forum and blog reports that a control change with the button's number and value 127 lights it and 0 darkens it, on the global MIDI channel (factory: 1), and that a few buttons have no LED (nickhwang.com, 'Korg nanoKontrol2 and Max', 2012)"],
    "channel": 1,
    "brightness": false,
    "off": 0,
    "styles": {
